---
import Layout from '../../layouts/SystemsLayout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Documentation & Guides | Sans Serif Systems">
  <div class="glow-blob glow-cyan"></div>
  <div class="glow-blob glow-purple"></div>

  <section class="page-header">
    <span class="meta-badge">KNOWLEDGE SYSTEM</span>
    <h1>Documentation & Architecture</h1>
    <p>
      Explore the frameworks, execution loops, public-private boundaries, and prototype roadmaps for AI-assisted natural language programming.
    </p>
  </section>

  <div class="docs-container">
    <!-- Left Navigation -->
    <div class="docs-nav card-glass">
      <h5>Architectural Core</h5>
      <a href="/docs/natural-language-programming-stack/" class="active">NLP Systems Stack</a>
      <a href="/docs/public-private-boundary/">Public / Private Boundary</a>
      <a href="/docs/tool-status/">Tool Status Registry</a>
      <a href="/docs/">Introduction</a>
    </div>

    <!-- Main Content -->
    <div class="docs-main card-glass">
      <section id="intro" class="docs-section">
        <h2>Introduction</h2>
        <p>
          Sans Serif Systems is a solo-builder systems laboratory and utility bench dedicated to making AI-assisted developer operations predictable, verifiable, and secure.
        </p>
        <p>
          Our development philosophy rejects raw, ad-hoc, untracked prompt snippets in favor of formal execution loops, structured interfaces, and strict build ledgers.
        </p>

        <h3 style="margin-top: 2rem; color: var(--text-primary);">Three Operational Pillars</h3>
        <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(260px, 1fr)); gap: 1.5rem; margin-top: 1.5rem;">
          <div class="pillar-card" style="border: 1px solid var(--card-border); padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 8px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.01);">
            <h4 style="color: var(--accent-cyan); font-family: var(--font-heading); margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">1. Bounded Autonomy</h4>
            <p style="font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.5;">Limiting agent action spaces using declarative runtime schemas rather than raw system instructions.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="pillar-card" style="border: 1px solid var(--card-border); padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 8px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.01);">
            <h4 style="color: var(--accent-purple); font-family: var(--font-heading); margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">2. Proof of Evidence</h4>
            <p style="font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.5;">Logging verification output checks to an immutable local ledger before promoting files to main.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="pillar-card" style="border: 1px solid var(--card-border); padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 8px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.01);">
            <h4 style="color: var(--accent-orange); font-family: var(--font-heading); margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">3. Local-First Execution</h4>
            <p style="font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.5;">Enforcing local-first schemas, local tokenizers, and sandbox executions before hitting external networks.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h3 style="margin-top: 3.5rem; color: var(--text-primary); font-family: var(--font-heading);">Explore the Systems Docs</h3>
        <p style="margin-top: 0.5rem; line-height: 1.6;">
          Select a guide from the sidebar or get started directly by reading about the <a href="/docs/natural-language-programming-stack/" style="color: var(--accent-cyan); text-decoration: none; font-weight: 500;">Natural Language Programming Stack &rarr;</a>
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .page-header {
    text-align: center;
    padding: 4rem 1rem 3rem;
  }

  .meta-badge {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0.3rem 0.8rem;
    border-radius: 99px;
    font-size: 0.65rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    background: rgba(0, 242, 254, 0.08);
    color: var(--accent-cyan);
    border: 1px solid rgba(0, 242, 254, 0.2);
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .page-header h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 4.5vw, 3.2rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .page-header p {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    max-width: 700px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .docs-container {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 280px 1fr;
    gap: 2rem;
    align-items: start;
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .docs-nav {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    padding: 1.75rem;
    border-radius: 12px;
  }

  .docs-nav h5 {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .docs-nav a {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    padding: 0.5rem 0.75rem;
    border-radius: 6px;
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
    transition: all 0.2s ease;
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
  }

  .docs-nav a:hover {
    color: var(--text-primary);
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03);
  }

  .docs-nav a.active {
    color: var(--accent-cyan);
    background: rgba(0, 242, 254, 0.05);
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .docs-main {
    padding: 3rem;
    border-radius: 12px;
    min-height: 500px;
  }

  .docs-section h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: 1.75rem;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .docs-section p {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .docs-container {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
